        "original_id": "18332ac1-adc8-55e8-bded-be1a33f0278e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chad Channing, Dan Peters, Dale Crover, Dave Grohl\n- Organizations: Nirvana, The Vaselines, DGC\n- Products: Son of a Gun (EP), Incesticide, Sliver, In Utero, In Utero, in Tribute, in Entirety\n- Topics: compilation albums, tribute albums, cover songs\n\nFacts:\n- Son of a Gun is the debut EP single by the Glasgow alternative rock group The Vaselines.\n- Incesticide is a compilation album by the American grunge band Nirvana.\n- In 1992, DGC re-released the song Sliver to radio to support the release of Nirvana's rarities compilation album Incesticide.\n- At the time of Incesticide's release, most of its material was already circulating in fan communities in lower-quality form.\n- Because Incesticide compiled songs from different recording sessions and periods when Nirvana lacked a stable lineup, it features four drummers: Chad Channing, Dan Peters, Dale Crover, and Dave Grohl.\n- The title song Son of a Gun and the song Molly's Lips reached a wider audience after Nirvana covered them on Incesticide.\n- In Utero, in Tribute, in Entirety is a tribute album by various artists to Nirvana's 1993 third and final album, In Utero.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "af8a840f-9235-50c0-a3be-06ee949616b9",
        "text": "Page: Son of a Gun (EP). Sentence: Son of A Gun is the debut extended play single by Glasgow alternative rock group The Vaselines.\nPage: Son of a Gun (EP). Sentence: The title-song of this EP came to a wider audience after Nirvana covered it, along with \"Molly's Lips\", on their compilation album \"Incesticide\".\nPage: Incesticide. Sentence: Incesticide is a compilation album by the American grunge band Nirvana.\nPage: Incesticide. Sentence: At the time, the majority of the material on \"Incesticide\" was circulating within fan communities (albeit in lower quality).\nPage: Incesticide. Sentence: Since the songs were recorded in different sessions and some were recorded when Nirvana did not have a stable formation, the album includes recordings by four different drummers: Chad Channing, Dan Peters, Dale Crover, and Dave Grohl.\nPage: Sliver (song). Sentence: DGC re-released the song to radio to support the release of the rarities compilation album \"Incesticide\" in 1992.\nPage: In Utero, in Tribute, in Entirety. Sentence: In Utero, in Tribute, in Entirety is a tribute album to Nirvana's 1993 third and final album, \"In Utero\", by various artists.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
